Reason: The vlan_id parameter is used directly as an index into a bitmap that has size based on VLAN_N_VID without any bounds check. A malicious or erroneous VF can send a VLAN id >= VLAN_N_VID, causing out-of-bounds memory access when set_bit or test_bit is called.

